      "writtenOn": "2024-08-01T22:10:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Those patches + revert of aosp/3179764 + disabling [this override](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/google/gfxstream/guest/vulkan_enc/ResourceTracker.cpp;l\u003d4247;drc\u003dd955dd6a527ce4565a137aef84288e9b5fe4787d) that forces `VK_IMAGE_TILING_LINEAR` was enough to make vkcube-wayland look nice... on AMD GPU.\n\nOn Intel, I didn\u0027t manage to get it to work so far. When I hacked in [support for `VkDrmFormatModifierPropertiesListEXT`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/mesa3d/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_drm.c;l\u003d518;drc\u003d0bee32a4c393b7d989ca984101d6f07993b8d3f8), then [`VkImageDrmFormatModifierListCreateInfoEXT`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:external/mesa3d/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_drm.c;l\u003d616;drc\u003d0bee32a4c393b7d989ca984101d6f07993b8d3f8), and finally ended up with host-side Vulkan dispatch table not having `vkGetImageDrmFormatModifierPropertiesEXT` (needed from [`wsi_create_native_image_mem`](https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:hardware/google/gfxstream/guest/mesa/src/vulkan/wsi/wsi_common_drm.c;l\u003d521;drc\u003dde9d4474dcdfba692286968aab7ef8c5149ab6b1)) - the driver not supporting it, maybe? OTOH `objdump` shows me there\u0027s a `vk_common_GetImageDrmFormatModifierPropertiesEXT` in the .so.\n\nI can clean up the CLs with the changes and post them tomorrow if they may be useful anyway.",
      "parentUuid": "31f4ece9_441e738b",
